239	        // specifically for Payment settings (which includes the upsell section). When the
240	        // General save fires, it posts a JSON payload that has no upsell keys — ASP.NET
241	        // deserialises those as C# defaults. A naked ReplaceOneAsync would then stomp the
242	        // admin's carefully-configured upsell settings.
243	        //
244	        // Detection heuristic: if every upsell field in the incoming document is at its
245	        // C# default AND the payload has no custom headline copy, treat the section as
246	        // "not submitted" and carry the current DB values forward.  The Payments save
247	        // always sends explicit values (even when they happen to equal the defaults), so
248	        // the only way all of these are simultaneously at the coded defaults is when the
249	        // caller was a partial-payload save button that omitted the whole upsell block.
250	        PreserveUpsellFieldsIfAbsent(update, current);
