`/packages` is the real route. Here's your flow. It's three messages: an opening **language selector** (postback buttons), which branches into an **English** and a **Vietnamese** menu, each offering **Pricing**, **Group class**, and **Private class** as direct links.

## 1. Opening message — language choice (paste this as your flow's first message)

```json
{
  "message": {
    "attachment": {
      "type": "template",
      "payload": {
        "template_type": "button",
        "text": "Welcome to Soul Pilates! 🧘 Please choose your language.\n\nChào mừng bạn đến Soul Pilates! Vui lòng chọn ngôn ngữ.",
        "buttons": [
          { "type": "postback", "title": "English 🇬🇧", "payload": "LANG_EN" },
          { "type": "postback", "title": "Tiếng Việt 🇻🇳", "payload": "LANG_VI" }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## 2. English branch (connect to the `LANG_EN` payload)

```json
{
  "message": {
    "attachment": {
      "type": "template",
      "payload": {
        "template_type": "button",
        "text": "Great! How can we help you today?",
        "buttons": [
          { "type": "web_url", "title": "💰 Pricing & Packages", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/packages/" },
          { "type": "web_url", "title": "🧘 Book a Group Class", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/booking/" },
          { "type": "web_url", "title": "👤 Book a Private Class", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/booking/?format=PRIVATE" }
