## How the branching works
- The two **postback** buttons (`LANG_EN` / `LANG_VI`) are wired inside Meta's Chat builder: after pasting message 1, connect each button to the matching branch message (2 or 3). Meta hosts this routing — **no backend needed**.
- The three menu buttons are **`web_url`** links, so they open your booking/pricing pages directly and reliably.

## Two things to note
1. **Button limit:** Meta's button template allows **max 3 buttons** per message — this flow uses exactly that (2 for language, 3 for each menu), so you're at the ceiling. If you later want more options (e.g. "Talk to a human"), you'd need a second message or quick replies.
2. **Pricing URL:** I used `https://soulpilates.com.vn/packages/` (your real packages page). Swap it if you'd rather point pricing somewhere else.

Want me to add **UTM tracking** to the links (so these Messenger bookings show up tagged in your analytics, like we did for Google Ads), or add a **"Talk to our team"** option that hands off to a human?

Meta's paste box takes **one message**, and the Send API has no way to nest "ask, then branch" into a single message without postback wiring. The clean way to get everything in **one JSON that works standalone** is a **carousel (generic template)** — one card per language, each with its three options as direct links. Here it is:

```json
{
  "message": {
    "attachment": {
      "type": "template",
      "payload": {
        "template_type": "generic",
        "elements": [
          {
            "title": "Welcome to Soul Pilates 🧘 — English",
            "subtitle": "Choose an option below. Swipe right for Tiếng Việt →",
            "buttons": [
              { "type": "web_url", "title": "💰 Pricing & Packages", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/packages/" },
              { "type": "web_url", "title": "🧘 Book a Group Class", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/booking/" },
              { "type": "web_url", "title": "👤 Book a Private Class", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/booking/?format=PRIVATE" }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Chào mừng đến Soul Pilates 🧘 — Tiếng Việt",
            "subtitle": "Chọn một tùy chọn bên dưới.",
            "buttons": [
              { "type": "web_url", "title": "💰 Bảng giá & Gói tập", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/packages/" },
              { "type": "web_url", "title": "🧘 Đặt lớp nhóm", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/booking/" },
              { "type": "web_url", "title": "👤 Đặt lớp riêng", "url": "https://soulpilates.com.vn/booking/?format=PRIVATE" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**How it appears:** a swipeable two-card carousel — card 1 English options, card 2 Vietnamese — each with Pricing / Group / Private as tappable link buttons. All `web_url`, so no postback wiring and no backend.

**Trade-off vs. the earlier version:** this shows both languages as two cards side-by-side rather than *asking* the language first and routing. That's the cost of fitting it into one self-contained JSON. If you specifically want the "ask language → branch" gate, that genuinely needs the 3 separate messages connected in Meta's visual builder (postback can't be collapsed into one paste reliably).

Want me to:
