**One honest caveat:** this is genuinely everything in one JSON, but a *single* message can't branch on its own — the language chips (`LANG_EN` / `LANG_VI`) only route to different follow-up messages if your partner app lets you connect them in its flow editor. In one standalone paste, the buttons work immediately (direct links) and the language chips are just present. If your partner app can wire quick-reply payloads to next steps, use the 3-message flow I gave; if it only takes one paste, this is the maximum you can fit together.

